Do you pay attention to the details and thrive in the dynamic rhythm of shifting schedules? If so, this role is tailor-made for you!

Dive into proofreading-focused tasks (no content creation required) spanning diverse APAC industries, crafting polished news pieces at PR Newswire while immersing yourself in the realms of Public Relations and Media.

What we offer

• Hybrid working in Kuala Lumpur

• Permanent, Full-time, Employee role

• Immerse in an MNC culture

• Great exposure to regions across APAC

• Enjoy the company's medical insurance coverage

• All the statutory social contributions (SOCSO, EIS, and EPF)

• Statutory Public holiday

• Annual leave (12 days a year)

• Company Holiday (Wellness day 1 day per quarter)

• 24/7 Employee Assistance Program

• 5 days a week, 8 hours a day plus 1 hour break

• Proofread focused (no content creation required)

• Access to the latest news curated by professional writers from across various industries and key markets in APAC

Primary Duties &amp; Responsibilities

• Format client press releases, proofread documents with speed and accuracy;

• Offer professional suggestions to customers on how to improve their press releases;

• Ensure all client requests are handled to the highest customer service standards;

• Ensure that the team's routine workflow runs smoothly and that tasks are managed properly;

• Obtain and maintain a thorough understanding of distribution platforms and processes;

• Maintain seamless collaboration with colleagues in other functions and provide help as needed;

• Provide regular feedback on operational activities to the supervisor.

&nbsp;

Desired Skills and Experience

• 1 year of working experience is preferred, Fresh Graduates are also welcome to apply

• Fluency in English and Mandarin communication, including reading and writing both Traditional and Simplified Chinese, is required to communicate effectively with our APAC clients.

• Highly self-motivated and independent

&nbsp;

Work Arrangements

• 5 days a week, 8 hours a day plus 1 hour break time;

• Comfortable for overnight working, from 10 pm to 7 am

• Comfortable for a roster that may cover weekends, for example, Wednesday to Sunday, or Saturday to Wednesday

• Successful hire will be trained during daytime office hours for the first few weeks

